WEBVTT

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:05.169
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.507
Hello?

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:15.611
Computer, who activated

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.980
the emergency medical
holographic program?

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.314
Auto-initiation
of the EMH program

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:23.413
occurred when a shipwide
Red Alert was initiated.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:26.152
Emergency?

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.160
Sick Bay to Bridge.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:31.959
Captain Janeway, please respond.

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:34.626
Captain Janeway
is not on board the ship.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.658
Well, then, who's in command?

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:40.298
Internal scans indicate
no crew members are on board.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:44.242
You mean, the ship's empty?

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:45.801
Affirmative.

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:38.086
What is
the crew's current location?

00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:39.091
Unknown.

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:40.592
Did they go on shore leave?

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:43.561
Are they dead? What?

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:46.087
That information
is not available.

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:48.566
Can you give me
a ship's status report?

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.000
Affirmative.

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:52.333
Warp core is off-line.

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:54.430
The ship is restricted
to emergency power

00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:56.600
and auxiliary systems only.

00:02:56.642 --> 00:03:01.079
Structural integrity breach
on Deck 6, Deck 7 and Deck 12.

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:03.104
Deflector shields inoperative.

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:05.049
Weapons array off-line.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:07.177
Communications off-line.

00:03:07.219 --> 00:03:08.777
Sewage and waste reclamation...

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:11.051
All right, I get the idea.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.751
What caused this damage?

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:14.953
That information
is not available.

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:16.427
Of course it isn't.

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:22.227
Computer, transfer all
Bridge logs to this station.

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:23.758
Accessing Bridge logs.

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:26.067
Replay last log entry.

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:27.629
Heavy casualties...

00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:29.197
the warp core's going critical

00:03:29.241 --> 00:03:31.266
and the ejection system
is off-line.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:33.870
I've ordered all personnel
to abandon ship.

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.210
Lieutenant Torres and I...

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:43.649
Computer, have any escape pods
been ejected?

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:47.216
All escape pods
were launched at 2100 hours.

00:03:47.259 --> 00:03:50.251
Scan the ship
for any humanoid life-forms.

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:53.732
There are no humanoid
life-forms aboard this vessel.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:58.703
Well, I'm glad everyone bothered
to say good-bye.

00:04:10.414 --> 00:04:15.215
Chief Medical Officer's Log,
Stardate 48892.1.

00:04:15.252 --> 00:04:19.951
It appears that Voyager
has suffered a... disaster.

00:04:20.023 --> 00:04:23.220
What kind I don't know,
but one thing is clear.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:25.660
The crew was forced
to abandon ship.

00:04:27.464 --> 00:04:28.829
It would therefore seem

00:04:28.865 --> 00:04:31.095
that my usefulness
has come to an end.

00:04:31.134 --> 00:04:33.728
I am terminating my program.

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:36.534
If anyone finds this Log,
I can be reactivated by...

00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:40.999
Hello?!

00:04:56.193 --> 00:04:57.353
Hello?!

00:05:14.144 --> 00:05:16.738
Doctor!
What are you doing?!

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:19.772
Sorry. I wasn't expecting
a member of the crew.

00:05:19.816 --> 00:05:22.307
The computer said
everyone had left.

00:05:22.352 --> 00:05:25.185
The internal sensors
were damaged during the attack.

00:05:25.222 --> 00:05:27.156
They must not be reading
every life sign on the ship.

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:28.350
Attack?

00:05:28.392 --> 00:05:29.620
The Kazon.

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:33.323
Two of their Predator-class
warships took us by surprise,

00:05:33.363 --> 00:05:35.831
hit us with a volley
of plasma torpedoes.

00:05:35.866 --> 00:05:38.664
It started a core breach,
and we had to abandon ship.

00:05:38.702 --> 00:05:39.930
The Captain and I stayed behind

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:41.403
to see if we could
stop the breach.

00:05:41.438 --> 00:05:43.167
At the last second, we did.

00:05:43.206 --> 00:05:45.572
Why didn't the crew
return to the ship?

00:05:45.609 --> 00:05:47.804
Because they couldn't.

00:05:47.844 --> 00:05:51.541
The Kazon tractored all
the life pods onto their ships.

00:05:51.581 --> 00:05:54.015
They went into warp
before we could stop them.

00:05:55.085 --> 00:05:56.313
What's wrong?

00:05:56.353 --> 00:05:59.322
This tricorder isn't
registering your life signs.

00:05:59.356 --> 00:06:01.415
This one isn't working either.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.157
You've got to help the Captain.

00:06:05.195 --> 00:06:07.356
She was hit
by a falling support beam.

00:06:07.397 --> 00:06:08.659
I didn't want
to risk moving her,

00:06:08.699 --> 00:06:10.530
so I had to leave her
on the Bridge.

00:06:10.567 --> 00:06:11.932
Can't we beam her to Sick Bay?

00:06:11.968 --> 00:06:13.629
The transporters are down,
so are the turbolifts.

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:15.535
I had to crawl through
31 Jefferies tubes

00:06:15.572 --> 00:06:16.937
on five decks just to get here.

00:06:17.007 --> 00:06:17.939
Then you're going to have

00:06:18.008 --> 00:06:19.305
to go back up there
with a medical kit.

00:06:19.343 --> 00:06:20.503
I'll instruct you on how to...

00:06:20.544 --> 00:06:21.670
You don't understand, Doctor.

00:06:21.712 --> 00:06:23.737
I'm not going... you are.

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:25.577
I'm sending you to the Bridge.

00:06:25.615 --> 00:06:27.674
That would be ideal
if it were possible,

00:06:27.718 --> 00:06:29.686
but my projection
system is limited

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:30.846
to the Sick Bay
and the holodecks.

00:06:30.887 --> 00:06:31.876
Not anymore.

00:06:31.922 --> 00:06:34.152
For the past few weeks,
we've been setting up

00:06:34.191 --> 00:06:36.557
holographic emitters
on critical decks.

00:06:36.593 --> 00:06:39.653
We were hoping to set up
a remote holo-projection system,

00:06:39.696 --> 00:06:41.357
give you access
to other parts of the ship.

00:06:41.398 --> 00:06:42.956
Why wasn't I told about this?

00:06:43.066 --> 00:06:44.658
We hadn't even tested
the system yet.

00:06:44.701 --> 00:06:46.726
There was no guarantee
it was going to work.

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:47.737
I guess the Captain

00:06:47.771 --> 00:06:49.068
didn't want
to get your hopes up.

00:06:49.106 --> 00:06:51.074
Her compassion is heartwarming.

00:06:51.108 --> 00:06:53.440
The next time, I'd rather
be kept informed.

00:06:53.477 --> 00:06:55.445
Where are
these remote projectors?

00:06:55.479 --> 00:06:57.106
Decks 1 through 5.

00:06:57.147 --> 00:07:00.605
We also put them in Engineering,
the Mess Hall and the Cargo Bay.

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:03.016
All the projectors are in place,

00:07:03.053 --> 00:07:05.920
but the problem is, we're
going to have to interface

00:07:05.989 --> 00:07:07.513
with the Sick Bay
imaging system.

00:07:07.557 --> 00:07:10.287
That's going to take a lot
of power and computer memory.

00:07:10.327 --> 00:07:13.626
I don't know if we have
enough reserve power to spare.

00:07:13.663 --> 00:07:15.153
Most of the crew is gone.

00:07:15.198 --> 00:07:18.031
Could we divert power
from life support systems?

00:07:18.068 --> 00:07:19.933
Good idea.

00:07:20.036 --> 00:07:21.401
I can drop life support down

00:07:21.438 --> 00:07:23.338
to minimum levels
on the lower decks.

00:07:23.373 --> 00:07:25.341
That should give us
enough power.

00:07:25.375 --> 00:07:27.570
All right, I'll need
another 20 minutes

00:07:27.611 --> 00:07:29.306
to get the projectors on line.

00:07:39.656 --> 00:07:41.248
All right.

00:07:41.291 --> 00:07:44.783
The remote projectors are
charged and ready to go.

00:07:44.828 --> 00:07:47.956
Imaging interface... stable.

00:07:47.998 --> 00:07:50.364
Are you ready to try this?

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:52.766
I assume there's still
an emergency medical kit

00:07:52.803 --> 00:07:54.100
behind the Tactical console?

00:07:54.137 --> 00:07:55.104
That's right.

00:07:55.138 --> 00:07:56.332
Then I'm ready.

00:07:56.373 --> 00:07:58.807
There are a couple of things
you should know.

00:07:58.842 --> 00:07:59.866
In order to do this,

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:02.208
I had to recalibrate
your containment field,

00:08:02.245 --> 00:08:05.840
so your holo-matrix will be
very sensitive to disruption.

00:08:05.882 --> 00:08:08.180
Try to stay away
from energy discharges...

00:08:08.218 --> 00:08:11.016
phaser fire, force fields,
that sort of thing.

00:08:11.054 --> 00:08:12.885
- I'll try.
- Make sure you do,

00:08:12.923 --> 00:08:14.823
because, if your containment
field collapses,

00:08:14.858 --> 00:08:16.826
it'll take hours
to reinitialize your program.

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:18.851
Understood.

00:08:19.863 --> 00:08:21.194
I'm going to head down
to Engineering

00:08:21.231 --> 00:08:23.256
and try to get some
of the critical systems working.

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:26.235
You'll hear from me when I get
the com system back on line.

00:08:26.269 --> 00:08:28.669
Unless, of course,
this doesn't work,

00:08:28.705 --> 00:08:31.868
in which case, I'll see you
in about five seconds.

00:08:33.276 --> 00:08:35.141
Good luck, Doctor.

00:08:35.178 --> 00:08:36.873
Thank you.

00:08:36.913 --> 00:08:39.108
I have a feeling I'll need it.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:54.590
Well... it's bigger
than I thought.

00:09:08.044 --> 00:09:09.477
Captain?

00:09:45.415 --> 00:09:46.939
Hello, Captain.

00:09:47.017 --> 00:09:48.450
You're going to be fine.

00:09:48.485 --> 00:09:49.452
Oh, Doctor.

00:09:49.486 --> 00:09:52.250
I see the new holo-projectors
are working.

00:09:52.289 --> 00:09:54.450
Lieutenant Torres was able
to get them on line.

00:09:54.491 --> 00:09:57.949
Are you feeling any pain,
dizziness, nausea?

00:09:58.028 --> 00:09:59.518
I'm a little disoriented

00:09:59.563 --> 00:10:01.861
and I have
one hell of a headache.

00:10:01.898 --> 00:10:04.458
For some reason, none
of the tricorders are working,

00:10:04.501 --> 00:10:06.366
but, from what I can tell,
you have a concussion.

00:10:06.403 --> 00:10:08.928
I'd like to get you to Sick Bay
as soon as possible.

00:10:08.972 --> 00:10:12.237
The last thing I remember
is launching the escape pods.

00:10:12.275 --> 00:10:13.503
Lieutenant Torres and I

00:10:13.543 --> 00:10:15.511
were trying to stop
the core breach,

00:10:15.545 --> 00:10:16.910
and then I blacked out.

00:10:16.947 --> 00:10:19.415
You were successful in
preventing the breach.

00:10:19.449 --> 00:10:21.508
And the crew?

00:10:21.551 --> 00:10:24.645
They were taken prisoner
by the Kazon.

00:10:24.688 --> 00:10:26.713
Torres to Bridge.
Can you hear me?

00:10:26.756 --> 00:10:29.884
Yes, Lieutenant, we hear you.
Go ahead.

00:10:29.926 --> 00:10:31.188
Are you all right, Captain?

00:10:31.227 --> 00:10:33.627
Fine. I'm glad you
convinced the Doctor

00:10:33.663 --> 00:10:34.994
to make a house call.

00:10:35.031 --> 00:10:36.464
What's our status?

00:10:36.499 --> 00:10:38.729
I've got communications
back on line,

00:10:38.768 --> 00:10:41.703
and I think I can reactivate
the warp core, but it'll mean

00:10:41.738 --> 00:10:44.935
recrystallizing
the entire dilithium matrix.

00:10:44.975 --> 00:10:47.000
Keep on it.

00:10:47.043 --> 00:10:48.408
In the meantime,

00:10:48.445 --> 00:10:50.538
I'll see if I can restore
the Bridge controls

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.548
and start scanning
for the Kazon ships.

00:10:52.582 --> 00:10:53.776
Aye, Captain.
Torres out.

00:10:53.817 --> 00:10:56.786
Doctor, do you know anything
about bypassing a power relay?

00:10:56.820 --> 00:10:59.288
Is it anything
like a coronary bypass?

00:10:59.322 --> 00:11:00.880
Actually, it is.

00:11:00.924 --> 00:11:02.949
Give me a hand.

00:11:02.993 --> 00:11:04.893
See this conduit?

00:11:04.928 --> 00:11:06.190
It's a power relay.

00:11:06.229 --> 00:11:07.662
Its circuits are burnt out.

00:11:07.697 --> 00:11:09.130
What we need to do
is reconfigure...

00:11:09.165 --> 00:11:12.225
Neelix to Bridge.
Is anyone there? Emergency.

00:11:12.268 --> 00:11:13.235
Neelix, this is the Captain.

00:11:13.269 --> 00:11:14.236
What's wrong?

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:15.567
Help, I need help!

00:11:15.605 --> 00:11:16.731
I'm in the Mess Hall.
There's a...

00:11:17.774 --> 00:11:19.503
Neelix, are you there?

00:11:19.542 --> 00:11:20.975
Neelix!

00:11:21.077 --> 00:11:22.738
With the turbolifts down,

00:11:22.779 --> 00:11:24.770
it'll take me
a half hour to get there.

00:11:24.814 --> 00:11:26.873
Doctor...

00:11:26.916 --> 00:11:28.406
it's up to you.

00:11:28.451 --> 00:11:31.181
I'll use the remote projectors
to send you to the Mess Hall.

00:11:31.221 --> 00:11:32.711
Stand by for transfer.

00:11:37.293 --> 00:11:40.751
I hope that crushed your skull,
Kazon pus hog!

00:11:40.797 --> 00:11:42.321
Kazon?

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:46.330
What's it like to stare
death in the face, Kazon?

00:12:06.321 --> 00:12:07.720
Missed me.

00:12:17.365 --> 00:12:20.357
I suggest
you surrender now, Kazon!

00:12:20.401 --> 00:12:22.130
The Captain's on her way.

00:12:30.144 --> 00:12:33.671
Gut spore!
You needle snake!

00:12:46.594 --> 00:12:47.788
My best sauté pan.

00:12:47.829 --> 00:12:49.228
Good work, Doctor.

00:12:51.266 --> 00:12:52.358
You're injured.

00:12:54.669 --> 00:12:56.227
What's wrong?
Is it serious?

00:12:56.271 --> 00:12:57.465
Don't panic, Mr. Neelix.

00:12:57.505 --> 00:12:59.302
It looks superficial.

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:00.568
Am I going to die?

00:13:00.608 --> 00:13:03.133
Not unless you're
allergic to tomatoes.

00:13:03.177 --> 00:13:04.144
That isn't blood.

00:13:04.178 --> 00:13:05.338
It's some kind of sauce.

00:13:07.215 --> 00:13:10.207
Nondoran tomato paste.

00:13:10.251 --> 00:13:12.947
Ooh! That'll leave
a nasty stain.

00:13:13.021 --> 00:13:14.955
What are you doing here, Doctor?

00:13:15.023 --> 00:13:16.888
I could ask you the same thing.

00:13:16.925 --> 00:13:19.485
Kes and I were
on our way to the escape pod

00:13:19.527 --> 00:13:23.520
when this Kazon fungus came
crawling out an access hatch.

00:13:23.564 --> 00:13:25.964
I kept him occupied long
enough for Kes to get away,

00:13:26.034 --> 00:13:27.524
but he didn't give up so easily.

00:13:27.568 --> 00:13:28.592
So I took off running,

00:13:28.636 --> 00:13:30.263
he chased me,
and I led him here.

00:13:30.305 --> 00:13:33.172
No one gets the best of me
in my kitchen!

00:13:34.742 --> 00:13:36.266
I'm fine now.

00:13:36.311 --> 00:13:38.472
The question is, are you?

00:13:38.513 --> 00:13:39.741
Me?

00:13:39.781 --> 00:13:41.305
You're bleeding.

00:13:41.349 --> 00:13:43.476
Bleeding?

00:13:43.518 --> 00:13:45.383
That's impossible.

00:13:48.690 --> 00:13:49.816
Don't panic, Doctor.

00:13:49.857 --> 00:13:51.586
It looks superficial.

00:13:53.094 --> 00:13:55.119
I'm not programmed to bleed.

00:13:55.163 --> 00:13:57.996
Maybe you should
check your program.

00:14:01.169 --> 00:14:03.262
Emergency Medical Hologram
to Captain Janeway.

00:14:03.304 --> 00:14:04.601
Go ahead, Doctor.

00:14:04.639 --> 00:14:06.129
Captain, we've captured a Kazon.

00:14:06.174 --> 00:14:09.337
He's been rendered unconscious
and Mr. Neelix is fine.

00:14:09.377 --> 00:14:11.845
But I believe my program
is malfunctioning.

00:14:11.879 --> 00:14:13.710
I request that you return me
to Sick Bay immediately.

00:14:13.748 --> 00:14:14.715
Acknowledged.

00:14:14.749 --> 00:14:15.716
Mr. Neelix,

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:17.615
keep an eye on the Kazon
until I get there.

00:14:17.652 --> 00:14:18.676
I'm on my way.

00:14:18.720 --> 00:14:20.210
No problem, Captain.

00:14:33.801 --> 00:14:35.928
Pain?

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:38.336
I'm not programmed to feel pain.

00:14:45.546 --> 00:14:47.377
Heart rate?

00:14:47.415 --> 00:14:48.882
Blood pressure?

00:14:48.916 --> 00:14:51.009
Brain patterns?

00:14:54.722 --> 00:14:58.488
Computer, analyze emergency
medical holographic program.

00:14:58.526 --> 00:15:02.018
Has it been altered in any way
to include... life signs?

00:15:02.063 --> 00:15:03.655
Unable to comply.

00:15:03.698 --> 00:15:05.928
Requested program
is not on file.

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:07.490
Not on file?

00:15:07.535 --> 00:15:10.231
The program's running right now.

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:16.367
Display schematics for all
Sick Bay holographic systems.

00:15:16.411 --> 00:15:19.278
No holographic systems
exist in Sick Bay.

00:15:21.649 --> 00:15:23.583
EMH Program AK-1

00:15:23.618 --> 00:15:26.815
Diagnostic and Surgical
Subroutine Omega 323.

00:15:26.854 --> 00:15:28.913
Check the database
and you'll find it.

00:15:28.956 --> 00:15:31.550
Specified program
does not exist.

00:15:33.895 --> 00:15:35.055
Well, then, who is

00:15:35.096 --> 00:15:37.428
the Chief Medical Officer
on board this ship?

00:15:37.465 --> 00:15:40.366
The Chief Medical Officer
of USS Voyager

00:15:40.401 --> 00:15:42.369
is Dr. Lewis Zimmerman.

00:15:43.838 --> 00:15:45.305
Lewis Zimmerman?

00:15:45.339 --> 00:15:48.934
Yes. He was the engineer
who created my program.

00:15:48.976 --> 00:15:52.377
I understand he resembles me,
but he's not on Voyager.

00:15:52.413 --> 00:15:55.314
He's at the Jupiter Station
Holo-programming Center.

00:15:57.151 --> 00:16:01.144
Computer, how long
has Doctor Zimmerman

00:16:01.189 --> 00:16:02.918
served on Voyager?

00:16:02.957 --> 00:16:08.327
Dr. Zimmerman commenced duty
on stardate 48308.2.

00:16:08.362 --> 00:16:11.729
48308...

00:16:11.766 --> 00:16:14.929
That's the date I was activated.

00:16:15.002 --> 00:16:21.805
Computer, display all Starfleet
records on Dr. Lewis Zimmerman.

00:16:23.478 --> 00:16:25.412
He looks a lot like me.

00:16:25.446 --> 00:16:27.744
In fact,
he looks exactly like me.

00:16:27.782 --> 00:16:30.546
Computer, is this me?

00:16:30.585 --> 00:16:33.247
Affirmative.
Dr. Lewis Zimmerman.

00:16:34.489 --> 00:16:37.117
Doctor, we've almost got
the warp core back on line,

00:16:37.158 --> 00:16:39.058
but we need to know
where the crew was taken.

00:16:39.093 --> 00:16:41.186
I want you
to perform an ARA scan

00:16:41.229 --> 00:16:43.060
on the Kazon
while we question him.

00:16:44.332 --> 00:16:45.299
Is something wrong?

00:16:45.333 --> 00:16:47.961
Something's very wrong.

00:16:48.002 --> 00:16:53.235
These tricorders aren't picking
up any of your life signs.

00:16:53.274 --> 00:16:56.539
At first, I thought
they were malfunctioning,

00:16:56.577 --> 00:16:58.545
but now I find they show me

00:16:58.579 --> 00:17:02.413
to be a living, breathing,
bleeding human being.

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:03.610
What?

00:17:03.651 --> 00:17:05.141
And that's not all.

00:17:05.186 --> 00:17:07.450
According to the computer,
I'm not a hologram.

00:17:07.488 --> 00:17:10.457
I'm a real person
named "Zimmerman."

00:17:10.491 --> 00:17:12.322
I've been trying
to analyze my program,

00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:14.123
but the computer
says it doesn't exist.

00:17:14.162 --> 00:17:17.461
This could be a problem
with the remote projectors.

00:17:17.498 --> 00:17:20.797
The multiple holographic signals
may be confusing the computer.

00:17:20.835 --> 00:17:22.496
I'm going to deactivate you

00:17:22.537 --> 00:17:25.267
and then reinitialize
your program parameters.

00:17:25.306 --> 00:17:28.707
Computer, discontinue emergency
medical holographic system.

00:17:29.944 --> 00:17:31.673
See what I mean?

00:17:33.347 --> 00:17:34.371
You're right.

00:17:34.415 --> 00:17:36.940
Your program's
not anywhere on file.

00:17:37.051 --> 00:17:41.249
Computer, shut down
all holographic systems

00:17:41.289 --> 00:17:42.813
throughout the ship.

00:17:56.437 --> 00:18:00.271
Computer, what happened
to Captain Janeway

00:18:00.308 --> 00:18:03.004
Lieutenant Torres, Mr. Neelix
and the Kazon?

00:18:03.044 --> 00:18:06.138
All holographic simulations
were discontinued.

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:08.910
Simulations?

00:18:08.983 --> 00:18:11.918
Computer, I'm talking
about real people.

00:18:12.019 --> 00:18:15.284
Locate Captain Janeway.

00:18:15.323 --> 00:18:19.726
Captain Janeway is stored
in memory block 47-alpha.

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:23.594
List all other programs
stored in that memory block.

00:18:27.401 --> 00:18:30.234
This is
the entire Voyager crew.

00:18:30.271 --> 00:18:32.466
Computer, are you saying
that the crew is nothing more

00:18:32.506 --> 00:18:34.235
than a collection
of holographic programs?

00:18:34.275 --> 00:18:36.038
Affirmative.

00:18:36.077 --> 00:18:38.375
This is ridiculous.

00:18:38.412 --> 00:18:42.041
There must be something wrong.

00:18:42.083 --> 00:18:44.313
Doctor, am I glad to see you.

00:18:44.352 --> 00:18:45.910
Can you see me?

00:18:45.953 --> 00:18:48.285
Of course I can see you.
Who are you?

00:18:48.322 --> 00:18:50.654
Sir, it-it's me.

00:18:50.691 --> 00:18:51.885
It's Lieutenant Barclay.

00:18:51.926 --> 00:18:53.416
Reg... your assistant.

00:18:53.461 --> 00:18:55.224
My assistant's name is Kes.

00:18:55.263 --> 00:18:56.252
Who are you?

00:18:56.297 --> 00:18:57.264
Uh-oh.

00:18:57.298 --> 00:18:58.424
What?

00:18:58.466 --> 00:19:00.525
Oh, no.

00:19:00.568 --> 00:19:02.092
This is bad.

00:19:02.136 --> 00:19:04.604
This is... this is very bad.

00:19:09.110 --> 00:19:11.738
Don't panic.

00:19:13.981 --> 00:19:18.384
Uh... let's just try
to think our way through this.

00:19:18.419 --> 00:19:20.114
I'm not familiar with you.

00:19:20.154 --> 00:19:21.917
Are you a member
of the Voyager crew,

00:19:22.023 --> 00:19:24.116
or have we encountered
another Federation ship?

00:19:24.158 --> 00:19:26.023
Oh, boy!

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:28.028
The Voyager.

00:19:28.062 --> 00:19:29.495
Oh, boy!

00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:33.591
This is going to sound
a little crazy

00:19:33.634 --> 00:19:37.195
from your perspective,
but you've got to trust me.

00:19:40.308 --> 00:19:42.572
None of this is happening.

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:45.909
This is all
a holographic simulation

00:19:45.946 --> 00:19:47.709
that you've been running.

00:19:47.748 --> 00:19:49.113
What are you talking about?

00:19:49.150 --> 00:19:51.880
You're in the holodeck
at the Jupiter Station.

00:19:51.919 --> 00:19:54.752
Your name
is Dr. Lewis Zimmerman.

00:19:54.789 --> 00:19:57.417
You're a holo-engineer
and you've been running

00:19:57.458 --> 00:20:00.552
a program that's malfunctioning
and we've been trying

00:20:00.594 --> 00:20:02.118
to reach you.

00:20:02.163 --> 00:20:03.824
What are you saying...

00:20:03.864 --> 00:20:07.466
that I'm a... real person?

00:20:07.599 --> 00:20:09.931
Well, I always used
to think of you that way

00:20:09.968 --> 00:20:12.061
and I-I know
your wife tends to think...

00:20:12.103 --> 00:20:13.502
My wife?

00:20:13.538 --> 00:20:16.302
We'd, uh...

00:20:16.341 --> 00:20:18.434
we'd better take this
one step at a time.

00:20:18.477 --> 00:20:19.603
Please do.

00:20:19.644 --> 00:20:23.273
Well, uh, you see,
this, uh, starship...

00:20:23.315 --> 00:20:25.283
it's not really a starship.

00:20:25.317 --> 00:20:27.581
It was a program that you wrote

00:20:27.619 --> 00:20:30.486
to study
the psychological impact

00:20:30.522 --> 00:20:34.583
of long-term isolation
on a crew

00:20:34.626 --> 00:20:37.823
made up of Starfleet
and Maquis crew members.

00:20:37.863 --> 00:20:39.558
A program I wrote?

00:20:39.598 --> 00:20:40.826
That's preposterous.

00:20:40.866 --> 00:20:41.890
I'm the program.

00:20:41.933 --> 00:20:44.458
Voyager is a real ship,
manned by real people.

00:20:44.503 --> 00:20:46.334
I'm afraid not.

00:20:46.371 --> 00:20:50.535
This must have something to do
with the radiation surge.

00:20:50.575 --> 00:20:51.701
What was that?

00:20:51.743 --> 00:20:54.610
Well, we've been having problems
shutting the program down

00:20:54.646 --> 00:20:58.707
because of a kinoplasmic
radiation surge on the station.

00:20:58.750 --> 00:21:00.411
It's affected
all of the computer systems...

00:21:00.452 --> 00:21:02.511
including the holodecks.

00:21:02.554 --> 00:21:05.751
The radiation must be affecting

00:21:05.790 --> 00:21:08.054
the memory centers
of your brain.

00:21:09.461 --> 00:21:11.122
How did you get in here?

00:21:11.162 --> 00:21:12.390
Oh, I'm not really here.

00:21:12.430 --> 00:21:16.457
Clearly, I'm here
because we're talking.

00:21:16.501 --> 00:21:18.332
You see, what I mean is,

00:21:18.370 --> 00:21:21.362
I'm in a control booth
outside of the holodeck.

00:21:21.406 --> 00:21:25.934
What you see
is a projection of my body,

00:21:25.977 --> 00:21:27.342
so that we can communicate.

00:21:27.379 --> 00:21:29.973
We've been trying to get in here
or send a com signal in

00:21:30.015 --> 00:21:30.982
for nearly six hours.

00:21:31.082 --> 00:21:32.549
You expect me to believe

00:21:32.584 --> 00:21:35.519
that the past six months
I've spent on this ship

00:21:35.554 --> 00:21:36.987
have been nothing
but a simulation?

00:21:37.055 --> 00:21:38.955
You haven't been here
six months.

00:21:38.990 --> 00:21:40.924
You've only been here six hours.

00:21:40.959 --> 00:21:42.221
That's impossible.

00:21:42.260 --> 00:21:45.286
I have very clear memories of
my first appearance on Voyager,

00:21:45.330 --> 00:21:47.230
meeting Captain Janeway
for the first time...

00:21:47.265 --> 00:21:49.199
I've had numerous experiences
aboard this ship.

00:21:49.234 --> 00:21:50.997
That's all part
of the simulation.

00:21:51.102 --> 00:21:53.730
How do I know
you're not some type of alien

00:21:53.772 --> 00:21:55.740
impersonating
a Starfleet officer?

00:21:55.774 --> 00:21:59.938
Look, Doctor, it's
very important

00:21:59.978 --> 00:22:01.445
that you believe me.

00:22:01.479 --> 00:22:03.504
You're losing
your sense of identity.

00:22:03.548 --> 00:22:06.039
You're starting to think
that you're part of the program

00:22:06.084 --> 00:22:09.076
and that's... that's not good.

00:22:09.120 --> 00:22:11.520
It's called HTDS...

00:22:11.556 --> 00:22:13.581
holo-transference
dementia syndrome.

00:22:13.625 --> 00:22:15.616
So now I'm having
a psychotic episode.

00:22:15.660 --> 00:22:19.790
No. Yes! I mean,
maybe the radiation...

00:22:19.831 --> 00:22:21.822
Doctor, I'm sorry
I have to do this.

00:22:22.834 --> 00:22:24.301
How dare you?

00:22:24.336 --> 00:22:26.236
It hurt, right?

00:22:26.271 --> 00:22:29.399
If you were a program,
it wouldn't hurt.

00:22:29.441 --> 00:22:31.500
I-I could be programmed
to think it hurt.

00:22:31.543 --> 00:22:32.532
Doctor!

00:22:33.545 --> 00:22:34.671
I'll be back.

00:22:36.948 --> 00:22:38.939
I've got to discuss this
with the others.

00:22:38.984 --> 00:22:41.509
Don't... don't go anywhere.

00:22:45.056 --> 00:22:46.523
Pain.

00:22:48.526 --> 00:22:50.687
Pain.
Why would I have pain?

00:22:53.898 --> 00:22:55.661
I think I'm hungry.

00:22:55.700 --> 00:22:59.261
I'm not sure what for,
but I'm definitely hungry.

00:22:59.304 --> 00:23:01.738
This is impossible.

00:23:03.575 --> 00:23:06.874
The problem is worse
than we thought.

00:23:06.911 --> 00:23:10.278
The, uh, radiation is
disrupting the command protocol,

00:23:10.315 --> 00:23:12.476
so we can't
shut the program down

00:23:12.517 --> 00:23:14.178
and while the program
is running,

00:23:14.219 --> 00:23:16.710
we can't access
the holodeck grid.

00:23:16.755 --> 00:23:18.746
Why don't you
beam me out of here?

00:23:18.790 --> 00:23:20.951
We tried, but the radiation

00:23:20.992 --> 00:23:22.857
is interfering
with the transporters

00:23:22.894 --> 00:23:24.589
and we can't get a lock on you.

00:23:24.629 --> 00:23:28.622
I've consulted with our
neurologist, Dr. Kaplan,

00:23:28.667 --> 00:23:31.261
and he said that if we
can't get you out of here

00:23:31.302 --> 00:23:32.826
within the next hour,
that the radiation

00:23:32.871 --> 00:23:36.898
would completely oxidize
your neuro-cellular structures.

00:23:38.009 --> 00:23:40.978
So, what do you suggest?

00:23:41.046 --> 00:23:43.844
There's only one way left
to terminate the program

00:23:43.882 --> 00:23:45.179
and that's to play it out.

00:23:45.216 --> 00:23:48.344
Bring it to its conclusion,
and once the simulation ends,

00:23:48.386 --> 00:23:51.822
it'll release the access locks
on the holodeck arch,

00:23:51.856 --> 00:23:53.619
and we can get you out of here.

00:23:53.658 --> 00:23:57.253
How does it conclude?

00:23:57.295 --> 00:24:00.753
You programmed
two possible outcomes...

00:24:00.799 --> 00:24:03.700
either Voyager finds its way
back to Federation space

00:24:03.735 --> 00:24:05.930
or it's destroyed
in the process.

00:24:05.970 --> 00:24:09.337
But the simulation
was designed to run for weeks

00:24:09.374 --> 00:24:12.400
before either happens.

00:24:12.444 --> 00:24:14.605
But I know of a way

00:24:14.646 --> 00:24:17.080
that you can bring it
to an end right now.

00:24:17.115 --> 00:24:18.810
Destroy the ship.

00:24:18.850 --> 00:24:20.818
Destroy the ship?

00:24:20.852 --> 00:24:22.843
Destroy Voyager?

00:24:22.887 --> 00:24:25.481
This is just a simulation,
Lewis.

00:24:25.523 --> 00:24:27.821
None of this is real

00:24:27.859 --> 00:24:33.297
and unless you destroy this ship
that you think you're on,

00:24:33.331 --> 00:24:34.992
you're going to die.

00:24:44.209 --> 00:24:47.144
No. No, absolutely not.

00:24:47.178 --> 00:24:49.339
Doctor, it's the only way.

00:24:49.380 --> 00:24:52.781
First of all, I don't even know
how to destroy the ship.

00:24:52.817 --> 00:24:54.648
Second of all, I wouldn't
do it even if I could.

00:24:54.686 --> 00:24:57.246
And third, how do I know
you're not an alien intruder

00:24:57.288 --> 00:24:59.381
trying to trick me
into killing everyone?

00:24:59.424 --> 00:25:02.291
Well... those are
good questions.

00:25:04.863 --> 00:25:07.798
First, I can tell you
how to destroy the Voyager.

00:25:07.832 --> 00:25:10.733
Second, if you don't do it,
you're going to die.

00:25:10.769 --> 00:25:14.102
And third...
well, I'm just not an alien

00:25:14.139 --> 00:25:16.573
and I don't know how else
to convince you of that.

00:25:16.608 --> 00:25:20.169
If what you're saying is true,
why don't you destroy the ship?

00:25:20.211 --> 00:25:21.473
Why do I have to do it?

00:25:21.513 --> 00:25:23.310
You're the one running
the simulation.

00:25:23.348 --> 00:25:26.943
It's coded to respond
to your input, not mine.

00:25:27.051 --> 00:25:28.678
I'm sorry, Mr. Barclay...

00:25:28.720 --> 00:25:30.347
if that's what your name
really is...

00:25:30.388 --> 00:25:32.288
but you're not very convincing.

00:25:32.323 --> 00:25:34.518
Here. Use this tricorder.

00:25:34.559 --> 00:25:36.993
Scan the room out
to a distance of 15 meters.

00:25:41.299 --> 00:25:43.563
This appears to show
a wall 15 meters away

00:25:43.601 --> 00:25:45.432
and it does have a holodeck
grid configuration.

00:25:45.470 --> 00:25:46.437
You see?

00:25:46.471 --> 00:25:47.961
But you could be manipulating
these readings.

00:25:48.006 --> 00:25:49.337
Scan me!

00:25:49.374 --> 00:25:51.706
You'll see
I'm a holographic projection

00:25:51.743 --> 00:25:53.643
originating
from beyond that wall.

00:25:55.313 --> 00:25:56.746
Yes. All right.

00:25:56.781 --> 00:25:59.773
But it could still be
an elaborate deception.

00:25:59.818 --> 00:26:01.615
I can't take that risk.

00:26:01.653 --> 00:26:03.621
There has to be some way
to convince you.

00:26:05.857 --> 00:26:08.018
Oh, I know.
I'll be right back.

00:26:11.329 --> 00:26:13.229
Orderly! Here.

00:26:14.265 --> 00:26:16.324
Are you the Emergency
Medical Hologram?

00:26:16.367 --> 00:26:17.425
Yes, of course I am.

00:26:17.468 --> 00:26:18.958
Well, we've got wounded here.

00:26:23.641 --> 00:26:25.541
I've seen this patient before.

00:26:25.577 --> 00:26:27.306
He has multiple
percussive injuries.

00:26:27.345 --> 00:26:28.334
Tricorder.

00:26:30.181 --> 00:26:32.615
Medical tricorder.

00:26:34.786 --> 00:26:35.912
I've been in this moment
in time before.

00:26:35.954 --> 00:26:36.921
What?

00:26:36.955 --> 00:26:39.048
What are you talking about?
Help this man.

00:26:39.090 --> 00:26:40.921
Have we just been catapulted
across the galaxy

00:26:40.959 --> 00:26:42.620
to an unknown area
of the Delta Quadrant?

00:26:42.660 --> 00:26:44.525
- Yes.
- And you are developing

00:26:44.562 --> 00:26:45.824
tumorous growths on your chest.

00:26:45.864 --> 00:26:47.195
- What?
- Ah, so...

00:26:47.232 --> 00:26:48.756
that hasn't happened yet.

00:26:48.800 --> 00:26:50.233
Is this stardate 48308?

00:26:50.268 --> 00:26:52.236
Look, are you going
to help this man or not?

00:26:52.270 --> 00:26:53.237
I'm not.

00:26:53.271 --> 00:26:54.397
Mr. Barclay.

00:26:54.439 --> 00:26:55.633
The program must
be malfunctioning.

00:26:55.673 --> 00:26:58.836
Let me see if I can reset
the holographic projector.

00:26:58.877 --> 00:27:00.777
Mr. Barclay,
will you please return?

00:27:00.812 --> 00:27:02.177
Now do you believe me?

00:27:02.213 --> 00:27:04.909
This is the beginning
of the simulation.

00:27:05.016 --> 00:27:06.483
We can't shut down the program,

00:27:06.517 --> 00:27:07.609
but we can restart it.

00:27:08.820 --> 00:27:13.257
This is my first memory
of being activated on Voyager.

00:27:13.291 --> 00:27:14.918
Who the hell are you?!

00:27:14.993 --> 00:27:18.429
Did I program Mr. Paris
to be so annoying?

00:27:18.463 --> 00:27:19.930
Actually, I programmed him.

00:27:19.998 --> 00:27:21.932
I modeled him
after my cousin Frank.

00:27:22.000 --> 00:27:25.527
Hmm...
Computer, delete Paris.

00:27:25.570 --> 00:27:26.969
What are you?

00:27:29.607 --> 00:27:30.665
What did you do to him?

00:27:30.708 --> 00:27:32.676
Computer, delete Kim.

00:27:33.745 --> 00:27:34.939
Hmm.

00:27:35.013 --> 00:27:36.640
Are you convinced yet?

00:27:36.681 --> 00:27:39.946
Let's just say that your
credibility level is rising,

00:27:40.051 --> 00:27:42.747
but I'm still not prepared
to destroy Voyager.

00:27:42.787 --> 00:27:45.347
So what are you going to do now?

00:27:45.390 --> 00:27:48.723
I need to confirm
my true nature...

00:27:48.760 --> 00:27:52.389
whether or not I am
in fact a real person.

00:27:53.998 --> 00:27:55.829
Let's just say that I'm right

00:27:55.867 --> 00:27:58.062
and this is a real ship,
and I'm a hologram.

00:27:58.102 --> 00:28:00.662
If I were to destroy the
holographic memory core,

00:28:00.705 --> 00:28:02.468
then I should disappear.

00:28:02.507 --> 00:28:05.670
Yes, but if you destroy it
and you're still here...

00:28:05.710 --> 00:28:07.439
Then I'm not a hologram.

00:28:07.478 --> 00:28:09.113
And you'll know that I'm
telling you the truth.

00:28:09.113 --> 00:28:10.341
And you'll know that I'm
telling you the truth.

00:28:10.380 --> 00:28:12.439
The holo-memory core is
located in Engineering.

00:28:12.483 --> 00:28:14.041
Let's go.

00:28:17.087 --> 00:28:18.452
What's wrong?

00:28:18.489 --> 00:28:21.185
The remote holo-projectors
were taken off line.

00:28:21.225 --> 00:28:23.921
I shouldn't be able
to exist outside Sick Bay.

00:28:24.027 --> 00:28:25.358
That's because you're a...

00:28:25.395 --> 00:28:28.193
A real person. Yes.

00:28:28.232 --> 00:28:30.962
I'm getting the idea.

00:28:33.804 --> 00:28:35.237
Magnetic constrictors
are on line.

00:28:35.272 --> 00:28:36.398
The warp core is stable.

00:28:36.440 --> 00:28:39.409
Let's get started
on those plasma relays.

00:28:39.443 --> 00:28:40.910
You... who are you?

00:28:40.944 --> 00:28:42.775
I'm the Emergency
Medical Hologram.

00:28:42.813 --> 00:28:45.145
I didn't know you could be
projected into Engineering.

00:28:45.182 --> 00:28:46.649
I can't,
but it's a long story.

00:28:46.683 --> 00:28:48.082
I'd rather not get
into it right now.

00:28:48.118 --> 00:28:50.780
Fine. We have three wounded
crew members over here.

00:28:50.821 --> 00:28:52.288
I'm afraid I have
a more pressing matter

00:28:52.322 --> 00:28:53.289
to attend to, Captain.

00:28:53.323 --> 00:28:54.722
What do you mean, you have

00:28:54.758 --> 00:28:56.783
a more pressing matter
to attend to?

00:28:56.827 --> 00:28:57.851
And who are you?

00:28:57.895 --> 00:28:58.884
I don't recognize you.

00:28:58.929 --> 00:28:59.918
Oh, don't mind me.

00:28:59.963 --> 00:29:01.658
I'm just assisting the Doctor.

00:29:01.698 --> 00:29:03.131
Doctor, I am ordering you

00:29:03.167 --> 00:29:04.862
to take care
of these wounded crew members.

00:29:04.902 --> 00:29:06.893
Computer, delete Janeway.

00:29:08.338 --> 00:29:10.306
The program's not responding
to vocal commands.

00:29:10.340 --> 00:29:11.830
The protocols are
starting to freeze up.

00:29:11.875 --> 00:29:12.899
We don't have much time.

00:29:13.010 --> 00:29:16.571
Jarvis, Parsons,
put these men under arrest.

00:29:17.648 --> 00:29:18.774
Don't worry.

00:29:18.815 --> 00:29:20.339
Those phasers aren't real.
They're just holograms.

00:29:20.384 --> 00:29:21.351
I wouldn't be so sure.

00:29:21.385 --> 00:29:23.717
I was injured earlier.

00:29:23.754 --> 00:29:25.585
That means
the holodeck safeties are off.

00:29:25.622 --> 00:29:27.317
Now just a moment.

00:29:27.357 --> 00:29:29.018
Let's not do anything hasty.

00:29:29.059 --> 00:29:30.424
Who are you?

00:29:30.460 --> 00:29:33.054
Are you two responsible
for bringing us here?

00:29:33.096 --> 00:29:35.690
Actually, no.

00:29:35.732 --> 00:29:38.667
The Array you discovered
is controlled by an entity

00:29:38.702 --> 00:29:40.363
you will come to know
as the Caretaker

00:29:40.404 --> 00:29:42.269
or banjo-man.

00:29:42.306 --> 00:29:44.934
He's actually an alien life-form
who is caring for a species

00:29:45.008 --> 00:29:46.441
known as the Ocampa,
who live nearby.

00:29:46.476 --> 00:29:48.034
Enough.

00:29:48.078 --> 00:29:49.807
I don't know
what this is all about,

00:29:49.846 --> 00:29:52.041
but clearly, you're involved.

00:29:52.082 --> 00:29:53.481
Take them to the brig.

00:29:53.517 --> 00:29:54.848
I'll question them later.

00:29:54.885 --> 00:29:56.750
Mm, no, I don't think so.

00:29:56.787 --> 00:29:58.550
You're in no position to argue.

00:29:58.589 --> 00:29:59.556
I'm not arguing.

00:29:59.590 --> 00:30:01.285
I'm simply pointing out
that in several seconds,

00:30:01.325 --> 00:30:02.292
the entire crew of Voyager

00:30:02.326 --> 00:30:03.691
will be transported
to the Array,

00:30:03.727 --> 00:30:05.126
where you will be tortured

00:30:05.162 --> 00:30:06.959
and probed
for medical information.

00:30:07.030 --> 00:30:09.157
It will be quite painful,
but not fatal.

00:30:09.199 --> 00:30:10.496
Bridge to Janeway.

00:30:10.534 --> 00:30:12.502
We're being scanned
by the Array, Captain.

00:30:12.536 --> 00:30:13.901
It's penetrated our shields.

00:30:13.937 --> 00:30:15.063
What kind of scan?

00:30:15.105 --> 00:30:16.504
Bridge?

00:30:16.540 --> 00:30:18.405
Janeway to Bridge.
Respond.

00:30:22.279 --> 00:30:23.268
What are you?

00:30:24.281 --> 00:30:26.306
Time is running out, Doctor.

00:30:26.350 --> 00:30:27.442
The oxidation levels

00:30:27.484 --> 00:30:29.952
in your neural tissues
are rising.

00:30:29.987 --> 00:30:31.511
You've got to destroy this ship

00:30:31.555 --> 00:30:33.250
and bring this program
to an end.

00:30:33.290 --> 00:30:34.587
First things first.

00:30:34.625 --> 00:30:37.560
I have to make absolutely
sure what I am.

00:30:48.538 --> 00:30:50.563
This is the central memory nexus

00:30:50.607 --> 00:30:52.768
for all holographic systems
on board.

00:30:52.809 --> 00:30:54.367
If I destroy this,

00:30:54.411 --> 00:30:56.470
there won't be a single
hologram left on Voyager.

00:30:56.513 --> 00:30:57.878
Well, except for me.

00:30:57.914 --> 00:31:00.075
I'm being projected
from outside the simulation.

00:31:03.720 --> 00:31:05.347
Go ahead.

00:31:05.389 --> 00:31:06.583
Give it a try.

00:31:22.406 --> 00:31:24.271
Convinced?

00:31:26.276 --> 00:31:28.437
Computer, what is the status

00:31:28.478 --> 00:31:30.742
of the holographic
imaging system on Voyager?

00:31:30.781 --> 00:31:33.841
The holographic imaging system
has been destroyed.

00:31:33.884 --> 00:31:35.476
Are there
any holographic programs

00:31:35.519 --> 00:31:36.918
running anywhere on the ship?

00:31:36.953 --> 00:31:38.147
Negative.

00:31:38.188 --> 00:31:40.816
Then why is the ship still
here and not a holo-grid?

00:31:40.857 --> 00:31:42.825
Please restate the question.

00:31:42.859 --> 00:31:45.487
You said all holo-systems
were destroyed.

00:31:45.529 --> 00:31:47.622
Why is the ship simulation
still running?!

00:31:47.664 --> 00:31:50.428
All holo-simulations
have been terminated.

00:31:50.467 --> 00:31:54.233
Doctor, I-I know this
is a little confusing,

00:31:54.271 --> 00:31:56.535
but try to remember
that you just destroyed

00:31:56.573 --> 00:31:59.804
the holographic imaging system
on a holographic ship...

00:31:59.843 --> 00:32:01.606
a hologram in a hologram.

00:32:01.645 --> 00:32:03.442
If you want
to bring this to an end,

00:32:03.480 --> 00:32:05.573
you've got to destroy
the entire simulation...

00:32:05.615 --> 00:32:07.082
the ship itself.

00:32:10.220 --> 00:32:11.847
Then it's true.

00:32:11.888 --> 00:32:16.325
I am... a real person.

00:32:16.360 --> 00:32:18.794
And you're a person
in great danger.

00:32:18.829 --> 00:32:23.129
Destroy the ship
now, before it's too late.

00:32:24.735 --> 00:32:27.203
But if I'm wrong...

00:32:27.237 --> 00:32:28.932
Doctor, you've got
to believe me.

00:32:28.972 --> 00:32:30.963
What else can I do
to prove it to you?

00:32:31.007 --> 00:32:33.635
I know, I know,
but it's just so...

00:32:34.745 --> 00:32:36.440
There.

00:32:36.480 --> 00:32:38.971
You see what's happening?

00:32:39.015 --> 00:32:41.245
Holograms don't feel pain.

00:32:41.284 --> 00:32:45.687
Your brain is being flooded
with kinoplasmic radiation.

00:32:45.722 --> 00:32:47.451
You're dying.

00:32:47.491 --> 00:32:50.983
I... I guess you're right.

00:32:51.061 --> 00:32:52.119
Oh!

00:32:54.865 --> 00:32:56.127
What should I do?

00:32:56.166 --> 00:32:57.827
The warp core.

00:33:02.072 --> 00:33:03.437
Even set on full power,

00:33:03.473 --> 00:33:05.498
it's going to take
a sustained phaser burst

00:33:05.542 --> 00:33:07.601
to punch through
the outer duranium shielding.

00:33:07.644 --> 00:33:09.942
Set your phaser to maximum.

00:33:09.980 --> 00:33:12.847
Aim for the magnetic
constrictors.

00:33:15.385 --> 00:33:16.716
Ready?

00:33:16.753 --> 00:33:17.947
Ready.

00:33:18.021 --> 00:33:19.318
Stop!

00:33:19.356 --> 00:33:21.347
Doctor, don't listen to him.

00:33:21.391 --> 00:33:22.858
He's lying.

00:33:29.332 --> 00:33:30.594
Step away from the warp core,
Doctor.

00:33:30.634 --> 00:33:32.295
Don't do anything
that man tells you.

00:33:32.335 --> 00:33:33.597
You're in danger if you do.

00:33:33.637 --> 00:33:34.729
None of this is real.

00:33:34.771 --> 00:33:36.864
So I've been told.

00:33:36.907 --> 00:33:39.239
It's all
a holographic simulation.

00:33:39.276 --> 00:33:42.734
That's right, but it's not
the simulation you think it is.

00:33:42.779 --> 00:33:45.509
Everything around you is part
of a holographic projection

00:33:45.549 --> 00:33:47.346
that's being created
by your program.

00:33:47.384 --> 00:33:48.351
My program?

00:33:48.385 --> 00:33:50.979
You're on the holodeck
on Voyager.

00:33:51.054 --> 00:33:53.079
The Captain suggested
you take a day off,

00:33:53.123 --> 00:33:54.556
try a holonovel, so you did.

00:33:54.591 --> 00:33:56.889
But while you were running
the holonovel,

00:33:56.927 --> 00:33:58.554
there was a kinoplasmic
radiation surge

00:33:58.595 --> 00:33:59.562
in the imaging system.

00:33:59.596 --> 00:34:01.928
It created a feedback loop
between

00:34:01.965 --> 00:34:04.695
the holodeck computer
and your program.

00:34:04.734 --> 00:34:07.362
All of this,
including Mr. Barclay,

00:34:07.404 --> 00:34:09.531
is a holographic simulation

00:34:09.573 --> 00:34:12.167
generated by your codes,
subroutines

00:34:12.209 --> 00:34:13.369
and memory circuits.

00:34:13.410 --> 00:34:16.038
Don't be distracted by these
holographic characters.

00:34:16.079 --> 00:34:18.946
Stay focused
on what you need to do...

00:34:18.982 --> 00:34:21.212
destroy the warp core.

00:34:23.787 --> 00:34:25.254
Wait a minute.

00:34:25.288 --> 00:34:28.348
The entire crew of Voyager
was just taken by the Array.

00:34:28.391 --> 00:34:29.949
They won't be back
for three days.

00:34:29.993 --> 00:34:31.392
So what's he doing here?

00:34:31.428 --> 00:34:32.952
The program is malfunctioning.

00:34:33.063 --> 00:34:36.226
Are you the real
Commander Chakotay

00:34:36.266 --> 00:34:39.895
or a holographic projection
like Mr. Barclay?

00:34:39.936 --> 00:34:41.164
I'm a projection.

00:34:41.204 --> 00:34:44.105
I'm really at the holographic
control station in Engineering.

00:34:44.140 --> 00:34:45.903
You're trapped on the holodeck.

00:34:45.942 --> 00:34:47.876
We've been monitoring
the program from here

00:34:47.911 --> 00:34:49.936
and we've been trying
to reach you for hours.

00:34:49.980 --> 00:34:51.845
Sounds familiar.

00:34:51.882 --> 00:34:53.247
He told me the same thing.

00:34:53.283 --> 00:34:55.683
Doctor, do you remember
coming into the holodeck

00:34:55.719 --> 00:34:58.711
and running a holonovel
within the last six hours?

00:34:58.755 --> 00:35:00.586
No.

00:35:00.624 --> 00:35:02.922
No, I don't.

00:35:03.026 --> 00:35:04.493
That's because
your memory circuits

00:35:04.528 --> 00:35:06.291
are being eradicated
by the feedback loop.

00:35:06.329 --> 00:35:07.853
We have to get you
off the holodeck.

00:35:07.898 --> 00:35:09.798
Transfer you back to Sick Bay.

00:35:09.833 --> 00:35:12.131
You don't have memory circuits.

00:35:12.168 --> 00:35:15.194
You have a mind,
and it's being damaged.

00:35:15.238 --> 00:35:17.638
Destroy the Voyager,
the program will end

00:35:17.674 --> 00:35:20.108
and we can get you
off the holodeck.

00:35:20.143 --> 00:35:21.872
That's not true, Doctor.

00:35:21.912 --> 00:35:23.812
Because of the feedback loop,

00:35:23.847 --> 00:35:26.941
if you destroy the simulation,
you will be destroyed as well.

00:35:26.983 --> 00:35:28.780
Me?

00:35:28.818 --> 00:35:30.445
If you shut down
this simulation,

00:35:30.487 --> 00:35:32.955
your program will be wiped out
right along with it.

00:35:32.989 --> 00:35:35.685
There'll be no way
to retrieve the lost data.

00:35:35.725 --> 00:35:37.317
You'll be gone.

00:35:39.629 --> 00:35:41.529
Oh...

00:35:43.300 --> 00:35:45.564
Only real people
experience pain.

00:35:45.602 --> 00:35:47.365
You've got to believe me.

00:35:47.404 --> 00:35:49.964
What you're perceiving as pain
is really the feedback loop

00:35:50.040 --> 00:35:51.598
eradicating
your memory circuits.

00:35:55.245 --> 00:35:58.305
What...

00:35:58.348 --> 00:36:00.282
what is it you want me to do?

00:36:00.317 --> 00:36:01.284
Don't do anything.

00:36:01.318 --> 00:36:03.343
We're working on the
problem right now.

00:36:03.386 --> 00:36:04.478
We're close to a solution.

00:36:04.521 --> 00:36:08.548
Do nothing and you'll die.

00:36:11.591 --> 00:36:13.081
Doctor...

00:36:13.126 --> 00:36:14.093
trust me.

00:36:14.127 --> 00:36:16.721
Trust me, Lewis.

00:36:16.763 --> 00:36:18.355
Kes?

00:36:18.398 --> 00:36:20.423
Yes, you know me.

00:36:20.467 --> 00:36:21.832
You remember me.

00:36:21.868 --> 00:36:23.426
Yes.

00:36:23.470 --> 00:36:25.563
You're my assistant.

00:36:25.605 --> 00:36:26.936
I told you.

00:36:27.007 --> 00:36:28.565
His brain is being damaged.

00:36:28.608 --> 00:36:29.939
He's losing his memory.

00:36:29.976 --> 00:36:34.345
This is Kes Zimmerman,
your wife.

00:36:34.381 --> 00:36:37.316
This is all
a holographic delusion

00:36:37.350 --> 00:36:38.715
drawn from people
and experiences

00:36:38.752 --> 00:36:39.946
in your own memory circuits.

00:36:40.020 --> 00:36:41.510
You are malfunctioning.

00:36:41.555 --> 00:36:44.080
Lewis, please, listen to Reg.

00:36:44.124 --> 00:36:45.716
He's trying to help you.

00:36:45.759 --> 00:36:47.624
Destroy this program.

00:36:47.661 --> 00:36:51.062
If you listen to her, you'll
end up destroying yourself.

00:36:51.097 --> 00:36:53.793
Believe in yourself.

00:36:53.834 --> 00:36:55.392
You're not a program.

00:36:55.435 --> 00:36:59.132
You're a real,
flesh-and-blood human being...

00:36:59.172 --> 00:37:00.332
and you're my husband.

00:37:00.373 --> 00:37:03.501
I don't want to lose you.

00:37:06.246 --> 00:37:08.237
Lewis...

00:37:08.281 --> 00:37:11.375
how would you rather
think of yourself...

00:37:11.418 --> 00:37:14.251
as a real person
with a real life

00:37:14.287 --> 00:37:16.278
with a family that loves you,

00:37:16.323 --> 00:37:22.887
or as some hologram
that exists in a Sick Bay

00:37:22.929 --> 00:37:27.332
on a starship
lost in deep space?

00:37:27.367 --> 00:37:28.925
This isn't about what you want.

00:37:29.002 --> 00:37:31.835
This is about what you are.

00:37:31.872 --> 00:37:34.705
Just because you're made
of projected light and energy

00:37:34.741 --> 00:37:35.935
doesn't mean
you're any less real

00:37:36.009 --> 00:37:37.442
than someone made
of flesh and blood.

00:37:37.477 --> 00:37:39.638
It doesn't matter
what you're made of.

00:37:39.679 --> 00:37:43.115
What matters is who you are.

00:37:43.149 --> 00:37:45.379
You're our friend.

00:37:45.418 --> 00:37:47.784
And we want you back.

00:37:47.821 --> 00:37:49.311
Lewis, please.

00:37:49.356 --> 00:37:50.948
Pick up the phaser.

00:37:51.024 --> 00:37:53.151
Destroy the warp core.

00:37:53.193 --> 00:37:54.660
It's your only hope.

00:37:58.632 --> 00:37:59.724
Doctor...

00:37:59.766 --> 00:38:02.496
we're close
to getting you out of here.

00:38:02.536 --> 00:38:04.163
Try to hold on.

00:38:09.676 --> 00:38:11.701
Whatever happens,

00:38:11.745 --> 00:38:14.805
I just want you to know
I love you.

00:38:17.350 --> 00:38:19.250
I...

00:38:19.286 --> 00:38:22.119
I always wanted to tell you,
Kes...

00:38:26.026 --> 00:38:28.392
that you're beautiful.

00:38:30.163 --> 00:38:32.222
Thank you.

00:38:40.273 --> 00:38:41.934
What's going on?

00:38:42.008 --> 00:38:44.476
We were able to shut down
the holodeck simulation

00:38:44.511 --> 00:38:46.069
that your program
was generating.

00:38:46.112 --> 00:38:48.842
Commander Chakotay transferred
you back to Sick Bay.

00:38:48.882 --> 00:38:51.146
You seem to have
suffered no damage.

00:38:53.520 --> 00:38:55.147
What really happened?

00:38:55.188 --> 00:38:57.053
Voyager encountered
a subspace anomaly,

00:38:57.090 --> 00:38:59.285
which created
a kinoplasmic radiation surge

00:38:59.326 --> 00:39:01.021
throughout
most of our computers.

00:39:01.061 --> 00:39:02.585
Unfortunately, it happened

00:39:02.629 --> 00:39:04.597
while you were
using the holodeck.

00:39:04.631 --> 00:39:07.293
We've been working
for the past six hours

00:39:07.334 --> 00:39:09.029
to get you out of there.

00:39:10.136 --> 00:39:12.229
So, there was never
a Kazon attack.

00:39:12.272 --> 00:39:13.432
That's right.

00:39:13.473 --> 00:39:15.304
And the crew didn't really
abandon ship.

00:39:15.342 --> 00:39:18.106
No. In fact, except
for the computer problems,

00:39:18.144 --> 00:39:20.078
it has been an uneventful day.

00:39:21.615 --> 00:39:26.052
And who is this Lieutenant
Barclay I imagined?

00:39:26.086 --> 00:39:27.883
Barclay was part
of the original engineering team

00:39:27.921 --> 00:39:29.115
that designed your program.

00:39:29.155 --> 00:39:31.055
He was in charge of testing
your interpersonal skills.

00:39:34.394 --> 00:39:36.726
Oh.

00:39:36.763 --> 00:39:39.561
This should make
an interesting paper.

00:39:39.599 --> 00:39:40.725
Chakotay to Sick Bay.

00:39:40.767 --> 00:39:42.428
Is the Doctor all right?

00:39:42.469 --> 00:39:43.436
Yes, Commander.

00:39:43.470 --> 00:39:45.495
His program is
functioning normally.

00:39:45.538 --> 00:39:46.505
Good work.

00:39:46.539 --> 00:39:47.938
As soon as you're
finished there,

00:39:48.041 --> 00:39:50.407
I want all senior officers
to report to the Bridge.

00:39:50.443 --> 00:39:52.308
Acknowledged.

00:39:52.345 --> 00:39:53.903
It's good to have you back,
Doctor.

00:39:55.882 --> 00:39:58.214
Well... I suppose
I should begin cataloguing

00:39:58.251 --> 00:40:01.448
the niotrinate samples
I was working on this morning.

00:40:07.827 --> 00:40:10.193
So you really think
I'm beautiful.

00:40:10.230 --> 00:40:14.394
I was under a great deal
of stress, you understand.

00:40:14.434 --> 00:40:15.799
I may have said things

00:40:15.835 --> 00:40:18.463
that are not necessarily
my true feelings.

00:40:18.505 --> 00:40:20.973
Oh.

00:40:21.007 --> 00:40:23.373
Then you don't think
I'm beautiful.

00:40:23.410 --> 00:40:25.401
I didn't say that, exactly.

00:40:25.445 --> 00:40:28.471
I... I consider you very...

00:40:28.515 --> 00:40:32.212
very attractive...
in a platonic sense.

00:40:32.252 --> 00:40:34.880
I see.

00:40:34.921 --> 00:40:38.322
Then you don't really love me?

00:40:38.358 --> 00:40:40.986
I'm afraid not.

00:40:48.902 --> 00:40:51.268
Then I guess
our marriage is over.

00:40:51.304 --> 00:40:53.101
Our marriage?

00:40:53.139 --> 00:40:55.869
Are you making a joke?

00:40:55.909 --> 00:40:58.139
It isn't a joke to me, Lewis.

00:40:58.178 --> 00:41:01.705
I know we have problems,
but I think we can solve them.

00:41:01.748 --> 00:41:04.046
No.

00:41:04.084 --> 00:41:07.076
No... this-this can't be right.

00:41:07.120 --> 00:41:08.747
Something's wrong here.

00:41:08.788 --> 00:41:10.585
It's not too late, Lewis.

00:41:10.623 --> 00:41:12.853
You can still save yourself
by destroying the warp core.

00:41:12.892 --> 00:41:14.120
No...

00:41:15.862 --> 00:41:16.920
No, I don't believe you.

00:41:16.963 --> 00:41:18.931
None of this is real...
it's all a delusion.

00:41:18.965 --> 00:41:19.932
Somebody help me!

00:41:19.966 --> 00:41:21.695
I am helping you.

00:41:21.735 --> 00:41:22.702
Listen to him, Lewis.

00:41:22.736 --> 00:41:24.294
No!

00:41:29.409 --> 00:41:31.309
Doctor, are you
listening to me?!

00:41:31.344 --> 00:41:32.777
That man needs help!

00:41:37.851 --> 00:41:40.752
Try to calm down, Doctor.

00:41:40.787 --> 00:41:42.687
Everything's going to be fine.

00:41:44.958 --> 00:41:46.653
Doctor?

00:41:46.693 --> 00:41:49.025
Do you know who I am?

00:41:50.363 --> 00:41:52.763
Do you know where you are?

00:41:52.799 --> 00:41:56.701
I appear to be
on the holodeck grid.

00:41:56.736 --> 00:41:58.897
That's right.

00:41:58.938 --> 00:42:01.930
And do you know what you are?

00:42:02.008 --> 00:42:04.340
Yes. I'm...

00:42:04.377 --> 00:42:07.210
I'm the emergency
medical holographic program.

00:42:07.247 --> 00:42:09.579
Right?

00:42:09.616 --> 00:42:11.379
Right.

00:42:11.417 --> 00:42:15.751
Well, I assume
everything that's happened

00:42:15.789 --> 00:42:17.120
took place here on the holodeck?

00:42:17.157 --> 00:42:18.124
That's right.

00:42:18.158 --> 00:42:20.126
We encountered
a subspace anomaly

00:42:20.160 --> 00:42:23.061
and there was a radiation
surge in the computer system.

00:42:23.096 --> 00:42:25.963
And Kes is my assistant...

00:42:26.032 --> 00:42:27.795
not my wife?

00:42:27.834 --> 00:42:29.131
Your wife?

00:42:29.169 --> 00:42:31.501
Never mind.

00:42:31.538 --> 00:42:33.438
Captain, if it's okay,

00:42:33.473 --> 00:42:35.566
I'd like to return
to Sick Bay now.

00:42:35.608 --> 00:42:36.973
Of course.

00:42:37.010 --> 00:42:39.308
It's good to have you back,
Doctor.

00:42:39.345 --> 00:42:41.813
It's good to be back.

00:42:41.848 --> 00:42:45.079
Computer, transfer
EMH program to Sick Bay.

00:42:52.292 --> 00:42:53.850
We were married?

00:42:53.893 --> 00:42:57.420
It was a delusion, of course.

00:42:57.463 --> 00:42:59.988
I understand...
but I'd still prefer it

00:43:00.033 --> 00:43:02.467
if you didn't tell
Neelix about this.

00:43:02.502 --> 00:43:05.403
He tends to get
a little jealous.

00:43:05.438 --> 00:43:07.201
It'll be our secret.

00:43:09.175 --> 00:43:11.735
I am curious about one thing.

00:43:11.778 --> 00:43:12.904
What's that?

00:43:12.946 --> 00:43:14.106
The radiation surge

00:43:14.147 --> 00:43:16.138
caused my program to malfunction

00:43:16.182 --> 00:43:19.174
and my codes and circuits
began to degrade,

00:43:19.219 --> 00:43:23.417
and yet, instead of detecting
that threat to my program,

00:43:23.456 --> 00:43:25.856
I experienced
an elaborate delusion

00:43:25.892 --> 00:43:27.883
concerning the nature
of my existence...

00:43:27.927 --> 00:43:30.088
human or hologram.

00:43:30.129 --> 00:43:34.259
Person... or projection.

00:43:34.300 --> 00:43:35.824
Why?

00:43:35.869 --> 00:43:39.703
Why would my program focus
on such an esoteric dilemma?

00:43:39.739 --> 00:43:41.969
Well...

00:43:42.008 --> 00:43:45.967
I sometimes ask
those kind of questions.

00:43:46.045 --> 00:43:47.171
Who am I?

00:43:47.213 --> 00:43:49.807
What am I doing here?

00:43:49.849 --> 00:43:52.784
What's my purpose in life?

00:43:52.819 --> 00:43:54.582
Doesn't everybody?

00:43:54.621 --> 00:43:55.849
Not me.

00:43:55.889 --> 00:43:58.949
I know exactly who I am
and what my purpose is.

00:43:58.992 --> 00:44:00.789
I am
the Emergency Medical Hologram

00:44:00.827 --> 00:44:02.658
aboard the Starship Voyager.

00:44:04.931 --> 00:44:06.956
Are you sure about that?

00:44:45.138 --> 00:44:46.332
Hmm.
